#: mouse.cpp:438
msgid ""
"<h1>Mouse Behavior</h1> Here you can customize the way the KDE window "
"manager handles mouse button clicks. <p>Please note that this configuration "
"will not take effect if you don't use KWin as your window manager. If you do "
"use a different window manager, please refer to its documentation for how to "
"customize mouse behavior."
msgstr ""

#: windows.cpp:84
msgid "Windows"
msgstr "Vensters"

#: windows.cpp:99
msgid "Vertical maximization only by default"
msgstr "Vertikale maksimasie slegs by verstek"

#: windows.cpp:100
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, windows will only be maximized vertically while "
"keeping there width."
msgstr ""

#: windows.cpp:107
msgid "Display content in moving windows"
msgstr "Vertoon inhoud in bewgende vensters"

#: windows.cpp:109
msgid ""
"Enable this option if you want a window's content to be fully shown while "
"moving it, instead of just showing a window 'skeleton'. The result may not "
"be satisfying on slow machines without graphic acceleration."
msgstr ""

#: windows.cpp:113
msgid "Display content in resizing windows"
msgstr "Vertoon inhoud in dimensieveanderende vensters"

#: windows.cpp:115
msgid ""
"Enable this option if you want a window's content to be shown while resizing "
"it, instead of just showing a window 'skeleton'. The result may not be "
"satisfying on slow machines."
msgstr ""

#: windows.cpp:151
msgid "Placement policy"
msgstr "Plasingsbeleid"

#: windows.cpp:159
msgid "Smart"
msgstr "Slim"

#: windows.cpp:160
msgid "Cascade"
msgstr "Kaskade"

#: windows.cpp:161
msgid "Random"
msgstr "Lukraak"

#: windows.cpp:169
msgid ""
"The placement policy determines where a new window will appear on the "
"desktop. For now, there are three different policies: <ul><li><em>Smart</em> "
"will try to achieve a minimum overlap of windows</li> <li><em>Cascade</em> "
"will cascade the windows</li> <li><em>Random</em> will use a random "
"position</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#: windows.cpp:178
#, c-format
msgid ""
"  Allowed overlap:\n"
"(% of desktop space)"
msgstr ""
"  Toelaatbare oorvloei:\n"
"(% van werkskermarea)"

#: windows.cpp:192
msgid "Focus policy"
msgstr "Fokusbeleid"

#: windows.cpp:204
msgid "Click to focus"
msgstr "Kliek vir fokus"

#: windows.cpp:205
msgid "Focus follows mouse"
msgstr "Fokus volg muis"

#: windows.cpp:206
#, fuzzy
msgid "Focus under mouse"
msgstr "Fokus volg muis"

#: windows.cpp:207
msgid "Focus strictly under mouse"
msgstr ""

#: windows.cpp:211
msgid ""
"The focus policy is used to determin the active window, i.e. the window you "
"can work in. <ul> <li><em>Click to focus:</em> a window becomes active when "
"you click into it. This is the behavior you might know from other operating "
"systems.</li> <li><em>Focus follows mouse:</em> Moving the mouse pointer "
"actively onto a normal window activates it. Very practical if you are using "
"the mouse a lot.</li> <li><em>FocusUnderMouse</em> - The window that happens "
"to be under the  mouse pointer becomes active. The invariant is: no window "
"can  have focus that is not under the mouse. </li> "
"<li><em>FocusStrictlyUnderMouse</em> - this is even worse than "
"FocusUnderMouse. Only the window under the mouse pointer is active. If the "
"mouse points nowhere, nothing has the focus.  </ul>  Note that "
"FocusUnderMouse and FocusStrictlyUnderMouse are not particularly useful. "
"They are only provided for old-fashioned die-hard UNIX people ;-)"
msgstr ""

#: windows.cpp:234
msgid "Auto Raise"
msgstr "Outolig"

#: windows.cpp:238
msgid "Click Raise"
msgstr "Kliek lig"

#: windows.cpp:243
msgid "Delay (ms)"
msgstr "Vertraging (ms)"

#: windows.cpp:263
msgid ""
"If Auto Raise is enabled, a window in the background will automatically come "
"to front when the mouse pointer has been over it for some time."
msgstr ""

#: windows.cpp:265
msgid ""
"This is the delay after which the window the mouse pointer is over will "
"automatically come to front."
msgstr ""

#: windows.cpp:271
msgid ""
"Disable this option if you don't want windows to be brought to front "
"automatically when you click somewhere into the window contents."
msgstr ""

#: windows.cpp:630
msgid ""
"<h1>Window Behavior</h1> Here you can modify the way windows behave when "
"being moved or resized and KWin's policies regarding window placement and "
"window focus.<p> Please note that changes in this module will only take "
"effect if you use KWin as your window manager. If you do use a different "
"window manager, please consult its documentation on how to change these "
"options."
msgstr ""

#: desktop.cpp:76
msgid "Active desktop borders"
msgstr "Aktiewe werkskermgrense"

#: desktop.cpp:85
#, fuzzy
msgid "Enable &active desktop borders"
msgstr "Ontsper aktiewe werkskermgrense"

#: desktop.cpp:88
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, moving the mouse to a screen border will change "
"your desktop. This is e.g. useful if you want to drag windows from one "
"desktop to the other."
msgstr ""

#: desktop.cpp:92
#, fuzzy
msgid "&Move pointer towards center after switch"
msgstr "Plaas wyser in middel na verskakeling"

#: desktop.cpp:95
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, after switching desktops using the active borders "
"feature the mouse pointer will be moved to the middle of the screen. This "
"way you don't repeatedly change desktops because the mouse pointer is still "
"on the border of the screen."
msgstr ""

#: desktop.cpp:102
#, fuzzy
msgid "&Desktop switch delay:"
msgstr "Werkskermverskakelingsvertraging:"

#: desktop.cpp:104
msgid ""
"Here you can set a delay for switching desktops using the active borders "
"feature. Desktops will be switched after the mouse has been touching a "
"screen border for the specified number of seconds."
msgstr ""

#: desktop.cpp:121
#, fuzzy
msgid "Magic borders"
msgstr "Magiese grense"

#: desktop.cpp:132
#, fuzzy
msgid "&Border snap zone:"
msgstr "Grensverspringarea:"

#: desktop.cpp:133 desktop.cpp:144
#, fuzzy
msgid " pixels"
msgstr "pixels"

#: desktop.cpp:137
msgid ""
"Here you can set the snap zone for screen borders, i.e. the 'strength' of "
"the magnetic field which will make windows snap to the border when moved "
"near it."
msgstr ""

#: desktop.cpp:143
#, fuzzy
msgid "&Window snap zone:"
msgstr "Vensterverspringarea"

#: desktop.cpp:149
msgid ""
"Here you can set the snap zone for windows, i.e. the 'strength' of the "
"magnetic field which will make windows snap to eachother when they're moved "
"near another window."
msgstr ""

#: desktop.cpp:309
msgid ""
"<h1>Borders</h1> Here you can configure two nice features the KDE window "
"manager KWin offers: <ul><li><em>Active Desktop Borders</em> enable you to "
"switch desktops by moving the mouse pointer to a screen "
"border.</li><li><em>Magic borders</em> provide sort of a 'magnetic field' "
"which will make windows snap to other windows or the screen border when "
"moved near to them.</li></ul> Please note, that changes here only take "
"effect when you are using KWin as your window manager. If you do use a "
"different window manager, check its documentation for how to enable such "
"features."
msgstr ""

